7. WOW6432Node is not inherently suspicious

You'll see something resembling:

HKLM\SOFTWARE\WOW6432Node\...


Don't think:

Weird registry path = attacker.

WOW6432Node relates to Windows' handling of 32-bit applications on 64-bit Windows.

Same idea when you encounter:

SysWOW64


Those names themselves are legitimate Windows architecture artifacts.

