And the four analysis concepts you should know
Analysis	QuestionHashing	Which exact specimen am I dealing with?
Static analysis	What can I learn without executing it?
Snapshot/differential analysis	What changed after execution?
Continuous dynamic analysis	What did the process actually do while executing?

The most important lesson here is not AnalyticsInstaller.exe itself.

Never let one artifact determine your conclusion. Combine static indications with controlled dynamic observations, test competing explanations, turn confirmed findings into new IOCs, then feed those IOCs back into scoping.

That's exactly the same methodology you should eventually apply to suspicious uncommon binaries in your threat hunts, except in a client environment you obviously don't execute an unknown specimen on a production endpoint just to see what happens.
